  "Question": "\\[ \\frac{15^{30}}{45^{15}}= \\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\left(\\frac13\\right)^{15}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\left(\\frac13\\right)^2\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(3^{15}\\)",
    "E": "\\(5^{15}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "The exponent \\(30\\) is twice \\(15\\), so write \\(15^{30}=(15^2)^{15}\\). This makes the numerator and denominator products of fifteen factors that can be paired:\n\\[\n\\frac{15^{30}}{45^{15}}\n=\\left(\\frac{15^2}{45}\\right)^{15}\n=\\left(\\frac{225}{45}\\right)^{15}\n=\\boxed{5^{15}}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{E}}\\).",
